Subject: [PATCH] bsd_zero: no pc from signal contexts on iOS instead of aborting

Source:  manga_backup_converter source runners (U9), original work
Licence: GPLv2 (as HotSpot)

JVM_HANDLE_XXX_SIGNAL calls os::Posix::ucontext_get_pc() for every signal
before its SIGPIPE/SIGXFSZ ignore branch. On bsd_zero that function is
ShouldNotCallThis(), so a SIGPIPE (raised when a loopback replay server's peer
closed a socket) aborted the app with "Internal Error (os_bsd_zero.cpp:92)".
Return null on iOS: the ignore branch then runs, the pc-based branches are
skipped, and unrecognised signals still reach VMError.
---
diff --git a/src/hotspot/os_cpu/bsd_zero/os_bsd_zero.cpp b/src/hotspot/os_cpu/bsd_zero/os_bsd_zero.cpp
index a6225fe37..a269bd879 100644
--- a/src/hotspot/os_cpu/bsd_zero/os_bsd_zero.cpp
+++ b/src/hotspot/os_cpu/bsd_zero/os_bsd_zero.cpp
@@ -89,8 +89,17 @@ char* os::non_memory_address_word() {
 }
 
 address os::Posix::ucontext_get_pc(const ucontext_t* uc) {
+#ifdef __IOS__
+  // source-runner patch: the shared POSIX signal handler extracts the pc for
+  // every signal before it ignores SIGPIPE/SIGXFSZ. Zero has no meaningful
+  // pc; returning null lets those signals be ignored instead of aborting the
+  // app (a peer closing a socket raised SIGPIPE), and real faults still reach
+  // the error reporter.
+  return nullptr;
+#else
   ShouldNotCallThis();
   return nullptr;
+#endif
 }
 
 void os::Posix::ucontext_set_pc(ucontext_t * uc, address pc) {
